================================================================================
Data, weights, and results — NOT covered by the code license
================================================================================

1. PATIENT DATA IS NOT REDISTRIBUTED.
   This repository ships no patient data. Every cohort (Duke-Breast-Cancer-MRI,
   TCGA-BRCA, ISPY2 / MAMA-MIA, fastMRI-NYU) must be obtained by you, directly
   from its source, under that source's own Data-Use Agreement (DUA). This repo
   holds no DUA on your behalf and grants no rights to any patient data. See
   data/README.md for the per-cohort portal, license/DUA, and expected layout.
   The Apache-2.0 grant above does NOT extend to any cohort's data.

2. TRAINED WEIGHTS ARE NOT BUNDLED — HASH MANIFEST ONLY.
   No trained weights ship here. The large trained artifacts (~1.9 GB) are
   referenced by a checksummed manifest at results/TRAINED_ARTIFACTS.md, which
   lists a SHA-256 per real trained artifact and per frozen-feature input so you
   can locate and verify them once you have produced or obtained them yourself.
   The manifest is provenance metadata, not the weights.

3. RESULTS ARE PER-COHORT, WITHIN-COHORT, AND FIREWALLED.
   The reportable numbers in results/Table2_results.md are each a within-cohort
   result on its own patient-disjoint cohort. A number from one cohort is never
   pooled with, compared to, or juxtaposed against a number from another (LOCK-1).
   The claim boundary is documented in docs/CLAIM_LEDGER.md and enforced in CI by
   ci/ledger_lint.py.

4. SYNTHETIC DEMO OUTPUT IS NOT A RESULT.
   `make demo` emits synthetic control-sentinel numbers labelled
   "SYNTHETIC — NOT A RESULT": a forward-only wiring/integrity proof that the code
   runs, never a scientific claim and never real-patient data. Real results and
   synthetic wiring proofs are kept strictly separate (see README.md).

